A||||26||Leadfoot||What is the strangest fiero breakage you've ever experienced?||||12||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||09-13-2001||08:59 PM||||Mine has got to be up there.  On the way FROM work today, not only did my clutch give out and come back to life but the finger on the distributor rotor broke free.  Both of these occurred at the same time.  In the words of John Travolta...."Thas so weird!"<P>Had to edit cause I don't know if I am coming or going.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000001||Urchin||09-13-2001||09:02 PM||||I had my passenger side wiper and driver side headlight motor break in one evening.  Both fairly minor repairs, but annoying nevertheless  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/final.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||09-13-2001||09:28 PM||||Had an internal engine block freeze plug corrode through on my '87 GT V6. Pissed coolant into oil galley, all bearings wear toast in a matter of 15 miles. Only indication that something was going wrong was that temp was slightly up, oil pressure slightly up.<P>Ended up putting in a brand new '88 engine, purchased from a high school (3 years ago), as they were getting rid of 8 engines that were donated by Pontiac.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||09-13-2001||09:51 PM||||Changed my oil and filter, didn't check the old filter for a seal.<BR>Was driving home two days later and lost all my oil all over the road. Filled it back up and made it home, the next day I found out what I did   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Removed the the extra seal and all is well. Glad I was using thick oil.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||09-13-2001||10:14 PM||||I had a bent rear 88 cast suspension hanger thing...  that big huge cast iron thing.  yeah.  bent...  weird  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||x-thumpr-x||09-13-2001||10:31 PM||||Well, when I first got my fiero (given to me), the car had been sitting for three years. Turned into a bird feeder. Flat tires all around, slicks on the back. (was told he drove it like that in winter!) Starter bolts broken off (starter lying on cradle), rear right bearing gone & toe link rod. both fell apart when I replaced them . Previous owner actually drove the car this way for 6 months before he got another car. Also faulty distributor harness, Had to jiggle wire to work car sometimes. Replaced now.  Car runs nice now, except it has started eating more feul then normal last 2 weeks. Hmmmmmmm??? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000006||Cooter||09-13-2001||11:09 PM||||While making a hard left hander, my box of Krispy Kremes slid across the seat and broke my donut. Damn those leather seats!||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||09-13-2001||11:47 PM||||I had an Engine Cradle brake along the weld on the rear horizontal beam on an 86 SE 4cyl.  I took it in for an alignment and the tech called me out to the bay for a look.  That explained why the car wouldnt drive straight.....Needless to say I didnt get the alignment and had a tow truck haul the car home where we put the engine on a good cradle and gave the motor a good thorough engine out tune up.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ambush||09-13-2001||11:55 PM||||TODAY!!!!!!!!!! The Right headlight motor keeped spinning. after a while I just disconnected it. As soon as I finished that the left one started doing the same Fu***** thing. Now they are both on up.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Neal||09-14-2001||12:57 AM||||Broke my crankshaft<BR>cracked a head<BR>broke a sway-bar endlink (bought it that way, but VERY scary to drive over 80kph)<p>[This message has been edited by Neal (edited 09-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Leper||09-14-2001||01:55 AM||||My headlights have been up for so long (They were up way before I got the car.) That the springs that hold the headlight doors down wore out and one of the headlight door's hinges actually broke yesterday. I'm still debating weather or not to get some flushmount lights or just fix the old ones.<p>[This message has been edited by Leper (edited 09-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||09-14-2001||01:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>While making a hard left hander, my box of Krispy Kremes slid across the seat and broke my donut. Damn those leather seats!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You have to watch out for the white powered kind too.. thats what broke on me..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and we all know how THAT went hehe<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flag-sig.gif"> <FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flagnc-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Wolfhound||09-14-2001||02:24 PM||||I once went out and started a 2M4, drove about six blocks to a friends house. Stopped and found he wasn't home. The car then would not crank. I walked the six blocks back and found the starters outer case in the driveway.||||reg||7
Z||000013||HummelHund||09-14-2001||05:20 PM||||When I first got my 84' SE, it didn't have a heat shield for the rear part of the engine compartment. This led to my brand new pair of shifter cables being melted (ok, that's my fault). I got a heat shield off a junker and expected my problems to be over. It seems I didn't look at the routing of the positive battery cable around said heat shield. While driving home from school, the car starts stumbling, my check engine lights starts flashing, and the tach and voltmeter needles start bouncing around. I hear sparking type noises from the engine compartment and see smoke wafting out from under the vents. I pull over, open the decklid and notice that the positive battery cable has arc welded a 1 inch hole in my heat shield! The insulation on the cable had been worn off by the edge of the heat shield and when I touched it sparks shot out. We finally just electrical taped the offending cable and the car drove home like nothing had happened. It was almost worth all the trouble to see my father jump 6 feet straight backward when he touched the cable and it sparked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project/daily driver)<BR>'84 SE (Dad's Project)||||reg||10
Z||000014||Voytek||09-14-2001||05:23 PM||||Alternator belt came off once.  Nothing was loose and the belt did not break.  Some snow melted on the grille and water dripped onto the water pump pulley, then froze and there was no groove in part of the pulley, hence the belt came off.  I chipped the ice off, and put the belt back on.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fformula88||09-14-2001||08:48 PM||||I had the bracket that holds the alternator on crack on me.  I actually think a garage put too much stress on the bolt, but don't know for sure.  It took me 4 hours to replace it because I had to cut the alternator off of the other attachming bolt.  Ihe remaining peice of the bracket was too large to get out of the engine bay with the alternator attached!||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fierowrecker||09-15-2001||06:38 AM||||Hey Leadfoot!<BR>I had four breaks in my pelvis at the same time!<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||wkayl||09-15-2001||10:00 AM||||Pulled into a gas station to refuel.  Came to a stop and looked in the rear view mirror and saw SMOKE coming out of the engine vents.  After fumbling with the trunk key (in the excitement I forgot about electric trunk release) I opened the trunk and "poof", the smoke was gone.  It was just an alternator belt.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">   <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000018||LZeitgeist||09-15-2001||10:00 AM||||Damn, Fierowrecker... wasn't one good enough to suit ya? <P>You get a gold star for being thorough, I tell ya...||||reg||1
Z||000019||Jaygee79||09-15-2001||10:23 AM||||not really strange, but right now my A/C doesn't get as cold as it should and my heat doesn't get as hot as it should.  don't know what that is about.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Boomtastic||09-15-2001||05:32 PM||||In my now-long-gone '86 2M4, I broke a right side inner tie rod (ripped it right out of the steering rack!) while taking a hard turn in a parking lot. I heard it break, but it sounded like a suspension creak, and with 250k on the car she had a LOT of creaks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I drove the car 20 miles before I found out that the tie rod was broken! I only found out when I was going down a dirt road and all of a sudden the car slowed and took a quick left turn, even though the wheel was turned hard right. I got out, witnessed that both front wheels where pointed together like / \  , so I kicked the tire back into position and *drove* the car (around corners, down the highway at up to 45 MPH (anything faster and it started to wobble), etc!) to the dealership that I was working at. I got a ride home and into work the next day, and no one believed I drove it with the tie rod torn out. I had to drive it into the bay, turning the car like it was normal, to get anyone to believe it.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||pontiacs4me||09-16-2001||03:50 AM||||the bolts that hold the bracket, that holds the engine side of the dogbone engine mount came loose.  In turn while trying to make it home, the engine moved so far back when put in drive, it broke the neutral saftey switch wire that runs to the fuse block.  I made it home, fixed the engine mount, and the car wouldnt start, looked around for hours, the wire was encased in the plastic wire sheating, and coudnt see the break.  Its all fixed now.<P>oh and one more that happened thursday night.  I think this has to be the weirdest of all time.  I drove my fiero to Topeka to watch a friend of mine race at heartland park.  By  the time I got out of class and made it there he already broke an axle, so we had to tow the car outside the gates because they were going to lock the gates, and charge us admissions for the next day.  We bought a tow strap at the local parts store, and headed back to the track.  When pulling into the track, I tapped the gas to revv it up a little, and my throttle cable broke right at the gas pedal.  There was no way I could rigg it at the pedal so I took my console apart, took a razor, cut back the sheathing on the cable, and cut the cable.  I then hooked up a pair of vice grips on there and made a hand throttle.  ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Archie||09-16-2001||08:54 AM||||This didn't really happen to me but it happened to one of my cars that was being driven by one of my guys (Martin), and I saw it all happen because I was following it in another car. <P>Because of another small car problem, We ended up taking a 86 "T" top V-8 car to the Dells show this year. We had just finished the V-8 swap before that show. On the trip back home from the show heading East on I-90 Martin had a couple of races with this guy in a LS1 Trans Am. Here is what happened, leaving one of the Toll booths this T/A pulled away just after Martin did and Martin accelerated up to 120mph and this T/A never did gain on him. At the next plaza the same thing happened. By the next plaze the T/A had worked thru traffic to get ahead of Martin. At the next toll plaza, this guy was waiting for Martin and they went head to head from there. They ran side by side up to about 120 or so then, according to Martin, he heard the LS1 "cutting out" & Martin pulled away from him. We figure the T/A hit the rev. (or speed) limiter. <P>Anyway, when we got off of I-90 we headed North about 6 miles to the shop and left the Fiero there. The next day while we were moving that Fiero around the shop at like 2mph the front lower ball joint broke.<P>We are happy it didn't break a few miles earlier.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000023||fierobaby||09-16-2001||11:05 AM||||umm I dunno if this is strange but my hood reales cable doesn't work...well it works... but you have to jiggle it like crazy to get the stupid thing to open....<BR>and then there is my annoying headlights the passanger side one was not working at all... so we switched the motor... and about 2 months later what happens!? The stupid headlight has to be manually cranked down... well heres my delema! I have to open the hood... so then its a fight and a half to get the ghetto hood to open and then close!!!!!! UGH! maybe its just a cqinkydink :-)<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="LETTER"> AIM: Fierobaby87<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Jaygee79||09-16-2001||03:49 PM||||this happened to me once.  we thought we had fixed my headlights.  All of a sudden one of them started going up and down by itself and the car wasn't even on.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Slammed Fiero||09-16-2001||06:17 PM||||I have bent 1 set of front spindles , and found cracks in another. This set is holding up well to the big tires and high load cornering<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
